# Accepted vulnerabilities — Trivy image scan (docker.yml)
#
# All four findings live in npm's OWN bundled dependencies
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules), not in the application
# dependency tree — Trivy reports zero findings for /app and /app/frontend.
#
# npm@12.0.2 is the latest release (no newer build bundles the fixed
# versions yet). Patching npm's internal tree at image build time is not
# viable: npm uses its own tar/brace-expansion during package extraction,
# and mutating that tree risks corrupting the npm installation the
# container's CMD ["npm", "start"] depends on.
#
# Runtime exposure is negligible: these modules only execute during npm
# package-install operations, which never happen inside the running
# production container.
#
# Re-evaluate on each npm release — drop entries once npm bundles
# versions >= the fixed versions listed below.

# brace-expansion 5.0.7 (bundled in npm 12.0.2) — fixed in 5.0.8 / 5.0.9
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# ip-address 10.2.0 (bundled in npm 12.0.2) — fixed in 10.3.1
CVE-2026-69192

# tar 7.5.19 (bundled in npm 12.0.2) — fixed in 7.5.21
CVE-2026-73566
